Do not rely only on client-side JavaScript to set page titles and metadata.

Evaluate the safest approach compatible with the existing codebase:

OPTION A:
Implement a proper server-side rendering or static rendering architecture compatible with the current React and Express application.

OPTION B:
Implement a reliable pre-rendering system that produces route-specific HTML using the existing published Firebase business data and updates generated content when the owner publishes changes.

OPTION C:
If a more substantial framework change is genuinely necessary to achieve reliable public-page rendering, first assess the migration impact and implement it only if the complete existing BMS, Firebase integration, authentication, ordering system and 3D components can be preserved and tested.

Do not blindly migrate the entire project.

Do not perform bot-only cloaking.

Bots and human visitors must receive the same meaningful page content.

Public content must remain synchronised with the existing Firestore source of truth.

